module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- type-formers — the type-level operations over the Phase-7 refinement
-- formers. set-algebra-to-fenel Phase 7 Step 1b (brief:
-- `workstreams/set-algebra-to-fenel/briefs/phase-7-step1b-normalize-type.md`;
-- probe: `notes/phase-7-step1b-step0-probe.md`).
--
-- `normalizeType : Type -> Type` — the MINIMAL type-level canonicalizer
-- (P7-5). The 1a smart constructors (`unionT`/`intersectT`/… in
-- type-foundation.ts) can build a NON-canonical refinement
-- (`$refined{base, SeUnion[SeEnum{1,2}, SeEnum{1,2}]}`); this rewrites it to
-- its denotation-equal canonical form so equality / dedup / printing / storage
-- see ONE shape per denotation.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE `$`-KEY BARRIER (the refine.fenel precedent this rides). A `.fenel`
-- body CANNOT author `$`-prefixed-key objects (`{$refined}` / `{$void}`): the
-- parser/evaluator treat a leading-`$` key as a special op. So this body works
-- over `$`-free MARKER records, and the TS wrapper (`dispatchedNormalizeType`
-- in engine-bodies-dispatch.ts) owns ALL `$`-key marshalling — it classifies
-- the `$`-keyed input type into a marker, runs the EXISTING `dispatchedNormalize`
-- on the inner `set` (reusing the proven Fenel SetExpr simplifier — the probe's
-- "boundary-delegates" architecture), and re-authors the `$`-keyed result from
-- the outcome marker.
--
-- THE DIVISION OF LABOUR (probe Q2 — load-bearing): `setAlgebraNormalize`
-- (Phase 2c, already Fenel) does ALL the SetExpr-internal work — it COMPUTES
-- every decidable set-op to a concrete normal form (enum ∪/∩/∖ → SeEnum;
-- interval ∩/∖ → SeInterval; disjoint/empty ⇒ SeNone; ¬¬A=A; flatten). `$diff`
-- NEVER survives (so the P7-5 diff→intersect∘complement rewrite is MOOT — no
-- action). So this body's ONLY net-new logic is the TWO type-ENVELOPE LIFTS
-- that the SetExpr simplifier structurally cannot see (it sees `SeAll`/`SeNone`
-- but not the enclosing `$refined{base, ·}`):
--   • `$refined{base, SeNone}` ⇒ `$void`   (refined-by-∅ = ⊥)
--   • `$refined{base, SeAll}`  ⇒ `base`     (refined-by-⊤ = base)
--
-- SOUNDNESS (probe Q3): keying the lift on the COMPUTED `SeNone`/`SeAll` tag is
-- automatically sound — `setAlgebraNormalize` emits them ONLY when emptiness /
-- universality is PROVEN, so an undecided intersect normalizes to a concrete
-- decidable set (never a bare `SeNone`). Both lifts are denotation-preserving
-- (verified via the Phase-6 trio: `$refined{Int,SeAll} ≡ Int`,
-- `$refined{Int,SeNone}` empty = `$void`). No per-call gate needed — unlike
-- `refine` (which NARROWS), `normalizeType` PRESERVES denotation.
--
-- The markers (NtRefined / NtVoid / NtBase / NtOther) are `$`-free plain
-- records — NO entity decls (the audit-green invariant; the refine.fenel
-- RefineInput/RefineOutcome precedent).
-- =========================================================================

-- normalizeType — the marker dispatcher. The boundary pre-normalizes the inner
-- `set` (NtRefined.set is already the normalized $tag SetExpr); this applies the
-- two type-envelope lifts. NtVoid (the $void fixpoint) and NtOther (a
-- non-refined type — MINIMAL: pass through, no deep structural recursion) return
-- the marker unchanged.
@label "type-former: normalizeType"
@description "P7-5 — the minimal type-level canonicalizer: dispatch the $-free marker the TS boundary built. NtRefined ⇒ apply the envelope lifts to the (already normalized) set; NtVoid / NtOther ⇒ pass through. The inner SetExpr simplification is delegated to setAlgebraNormalize at the boundary (probe 'boundary-delegates'). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "type-former" "phase-7"
@category "engine-internal"
normalizeType : (marker: a) -> b
normalizeType marker =
  if eq marker.tag "NtRefined" then liftEnvelope marker.base marker.set
  else marker

-- liftEnvelope — the TWO net-new type-level identities (the conceptual content
-- of Step 1b). `setv` is the ALREADY-normalized inner set (a $tag SetExpr); the
-- lift keys on its computed tag (sound — see the header). A surviving compound
-- set (non-adjacent interval SeUnion, interval SeComplement) or any concrete
-- SeEnum/SeInterval falls to the catch-all ⇒ stays `$refined{base, set'}`.
@label "type-former: liftEnvelope"
@description "P7-5 — the two refinement-envelope lifts: $refined{base, SeNone} ⇒ $void (refined-by-∅ = ⊥); $refined{base, SeAll} ⇒ base (refined-by-⊤ = base); else ⇒ $refined{base, set'} (canonical). Emits the $-free outcome marker the TS boundary re-authors. Sound by construction (setAlgebraNormalize only emits SeNone/SeAll when proven). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "type-former" "phase-7"
@category "engine-internal"
liftEnvelope : (base: a) -> (setv: SetExpr) -> b
liftEnvelope base setv =
  case setv of
    SeNone -> { tag = "NtVoid" }
    SeAll -> { tag = "NtBase", base = base }
    other -> { tag = "NtRefined", base = base, set = setv }
